{
  "id": "25292_haibi",
  "headword": "{配備|はいび}",
  "reading": "はいび",
  "romaji": "haibi",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "deployment; positioning; stationing",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "deployment; positioning; stationing",
      "explanation": "placing military forces, equipment, or resources in strategic positions for use"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "25292_haibi_ex1",
      "japanese": "ミサイルが{配備|はいび}された。",
      "english": "Missiles were deployed.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25292_haibi_ex2",
      "japanese": "{国境|こっきょう}{付近|ふきん}に{軍隊|ぐんたい}を{配備|はいび}した。",
      "english": "Troops were stationed near the border.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25292_haibi_ex3",
      "japanese": "{新型|しんがた}の{戦闘機|せんとうき}がこの{基地|きち}に{配備|はいび}されることが{決|き}まった。",
      "english": "It has been decided that new fighter jets will be deployed to this base.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Composed of {配|はい} (distribute, arrange) + {備|び} (equip, prepare). Primarily a military term for placing forces or weapons in strategic locations. Also used more broadly for deploying equipment or resources.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {軍|ぐん}を{配備|はいび}する: to deploy forces\n- ミサイルを{配備|はいび}する: to deploy missiles\n- {配備|はいび}{計画|けいかく}: deployment plan\n- {前方|ぜんぽう}{配備|はいび}: forward deployment\n- {核|かく}{配備|はいび}: nuclear deployment\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {配置|はいち}: arrangement, positioning — more general; can refer to arranging people or things in any context\n- {展開|てんかい}: deployment, development — also used for military operations but has broader meanings\n- {駐留|ちゅうりゅう}: stationing (of troops) — implies a longer-term presence in a location",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
